<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>66.0</apiVersion>
    <areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>false</areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>
    <decisions>
        <name>Is_Tactical_Depth</name>
        <label>Is Tactical (Depth &gt;= 3)?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Gates ladder seeding to Tactical-level campaigns only. Strategic (depth 1) and Operational (depth 2) rollup campaigns never carry CampaignMembers so seeding a ladder there is noise. Depth is a cross-object formula so it can't be evaluated in the entry filterFormula — checked here inside the flow instead.</description>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - Skip (rollup campaign)</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_Tactical</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.FQS_Hierarchy_Depth__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>GreaterThanOrEqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <numberValue>3.0</numberValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Is_Events_Category</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - Tactical depth</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Is_Events_Category</name>
        <label>Is Events Category?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Routes the flow to the event ladder (Invited / Registered / Attended / Declined) when Campaign Category is Events, otherwise to the baseline fundraising ladder (Solicited / Responded / Pledged/Gave / Declined).</description>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Sent_Status_Baseline</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - Baseline ladder</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_Events</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.FQS_Campaign_Category__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Events</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Sent_Status_Event</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - Event ladder</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Fundraising Quick Start: seeds the correct CampaignMemberStatus ladder on a new Campaign based on FQS_Campaign_Category__c. Renames the Salesforce-provided Sent/Responded defaults and inserts the remaining ladder rungs so reporting and data entry use campaign-appropriate labels. Only fires when Hierarchy Depth &gt;= 3 (Tactical level) — Strategic (1) and Operational (2) rollup campaigns never carry CampaignMembers, so seeding a ladder there is noise. Skips Fundraising Top Level Campaign (structural placeholder). Event ladder = Invited / Registered / Attended / Pledged-Gave (5) / Declined (4); baseline = Solicited / Responded / Pledged-Gave (3) / Declined (4).</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>FQS Campaign Member Status Ladder {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>FQS Campaign Member Status Ladder</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>OriginBuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordCreates>
        <name>Create_Attended</name>
        <label>Create Attended</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Adds the Attended rung (HasResponded=true, SortOrder=3) to the event ladder. Attendance is captured manually — gala check-in, event roster upload — not derived from a gift, so this status is never flipped automatically.</description>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Create_Pledged_Gave_Event</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>HasResponded</field>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>IsDefault</field>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Label</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Attended</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>SortOrder</field>
            <value>
                <numberValue>3.0</numberValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMemberStatus</object>
    </recordCreates>
    <recordCreates>
        <name>Create_Declined_Baseline</name>
        <label>Create Declined (Baseline)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Adds the Declined rung (HasResponded=false, SortOrder=4) to the baseline ladder. Marks contacts who were solicited but explicitly said no — distinct from unresponsive/Solicited so segmentation for the next appeal can exclude them.</description>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>HasResponded</field>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>IsDefault</field>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Label</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Declined</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>SortOrder</field>
            <value>
                <numberValue>4.0</numberValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMemberStatus</object>
    </recordCreates>
    <recordCreates>
        <name>Create_Declined_Event</name>
        <label>Create Declined (Event)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Adds the Declined rung (HasResponded=false, SortOrder=4) to the event ladder. Someone declining an event may still give — that's handled on the gift record, not by flipping this status.</description>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>HasResponded</field>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>IsDefault</field>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Label</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Declined</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>SortOrder</field>
            <value>
                <numberValue>4.0</numberValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMemberStatus</object>
    </recordCreates>
    <recordCreates>
        <name>Create_Pledged_Gave</name>
        <label>Create Pledged/Gave</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Adds the Pledged/Gave rung (HasResponded=true, SortOrder=3) to the baseline ladder. Kept as a single status because Campaign Member is a touchpoint tracker — pledge-vs-fulfilled nuance lives on GiftCommitment/GiftTransaction, not here.</description>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Create_Declined_Baseline</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>HasResponded</field>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>IsDefault</field>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Label</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Pledged/Gave</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>SortOrder</field>
            <value>
                <numberValue>3.0</numberValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMemberStatus</object>
    </recordCreates>
    <recordCreates>
        <name>Create_Pledged_Gave_Event</name>
        <label>Create Pledged/Gave (Event)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Adds the Pledged/Gave rung (HasResponded=true, SortOrder=5) to the event ladder. A gift on an event campaign is a stronger response than Attended and lives above Attended on the ladder. Written by FQS_Campaign_Member_Status_On_Gift_Transaction and FQS_Campaign_Member_Status_On_Commitment; never flipped by attendance data (attendance is manual).</description>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Create_Declined_Event</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>HasResponded</field>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>IsDefault</field>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Label</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Pledged/Gave</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>SortOrder</field>
            <value>
                <numberValue>5.0</numberValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMemberStatus</object>
    </recordCreates>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Responded_Status</name>
        <label>Get Responded Status</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Retrieves the Salesforce-provided Responded CampaignMemberStatus for this campaign so its label can be rebranded to Registered on the event ladder. HasResponded stays true, which is what we want for a registered attendee.</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Rename_Responded_To_Registered</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Label</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Responded</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>CampaignMemberStatus</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Sent_Status_Baseline</name>
        <label>Get Sent Status (Baseline)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Retrieves the Salesforce-provided Sent CampaignMemberStatus so its label can be updated to Solicited for baseline (non-event) campaigns. Renaming preserves IsDefault=true and avoids the one-default-per-campaign constraint that would trip a delete-and-recreate approach.</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Update_Sent_To_Solicited</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Label</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Sent</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>CampaignMemberStatus</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Sent_Status_Event</name>
        <label>Get Sent Status (Event)</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Retrieves the Salesforce-provided Sent CampaignMemberStatus so its label can be updated to Invited for event campaigns. Same rename-in-place pattern as the baseline branch.</description>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Update_Sent_To_Invited</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>CampaignId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Label</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Sent</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>CampaignMemberStatus</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Rename_Responded_To_Registered</name>
        <label>Rename Responded to Registered</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Renames the auto-created Responded status to Registered on event ladders. HasResponded stays true so cross-campaign response-rate reporting continues to include registrations. Filter-by-Id pattern (not inputReference) because the current API rejects inputReference+inputAssignments on the same element.</description>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Create_Attended</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Responded_Status.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Label</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Registered</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMemberStatus</object>
    </recordUpdates>
    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Update_Sent_To_Invited</name>
        <label>Update Sent to Invited</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Writes Label=Invited onto the fetched Sent record for event campaigns. Filter-by-Id pattern (not inputReference) because the current API rejects inputReference+inputAssignments on the same element.</description>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Responded_Status</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Sent_Status_Event.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Label</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Invited</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMemberStatus</object>
    </recordUpdates>
    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Update_Sent_To_Solicited</name>
        <label>Update Sent to Solicited</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <description>Writes Label=Solicited onto the fetched Sent record for baseline (non-event) campaigns. Filter-by-Id pattern (not inputReference) because the current API rejects inputReference+inputAssignments on the same element.</description>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Create_Pledged_Gave</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Sent_Status_Baseline.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Label</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Solicited</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <object>CampaignMemberStatus</object>
    </recordUpdates>
    <runInMode>DefaultMode</runInMode>
    <start>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Is_Tactical_Depth</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterFormula>AND(
    NOT(ISBLANK(TEXT({!$Record.FQS_Campaign_Category__c}))),
    TEXT({!$Record.FQS_Campaign_Category__c}) &lt;&gt; &quot;Fundraising Top Level Campaign&quot;
)</filterFormula>
        <object>Campaign</object>
        <recordTriggerType>Create</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
